0..70 Comment "//! A signal in one wire: its layout gives two joined lamps one level."
71..74 Comment "//!"
75..149 Comment "//! A type states that two of its constants are one value. A layout of the"
150..225 Comment "//! type must give those two constants one bit pattern. A layout that gives"
226..282 Comment "//! them two patterns tells one value apart from itself."
283..286 Comment "//!"
287..359 Comment "//! The layout is a module that models the theory of the signal, and its"
360..437 Comment "//! carrier is the terms of one wire. The rule is a member of the module that"
438..514 Comment "//! holds a path between the two levels. The encoder is a case on the lamps,"
515..591 Comment "//! and each arm names a member of the module. The encoder names the law, so"
592..623 Comment "//! the case respects the rule."
624..627 Comment "//!"
628..644 Comment "//! - see: #8333"
646..669 Comment "// `Signal` and `Wire`."
